   "rule_summary": "Manufacturers must report any death, serious injury, fire, or thermal runaway involving a home battery to the relevant regulator within 24 hours of becoming aware of it, with a preliminary incident report within 5 business days and a complete investigation report within 30 days. Other thermal incidents presenting a credible fire or injury risk must be reported to the regulator within 5 business days. Manufacturers must promptly notify affected customers when an incident indicates a material safety risk, and in any event within 5 business days of confirming that risk.",
   "comparison": "weakened by: scope",
   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must report any death, serious injury, fire, or thermal runaway involving a home battery to the relevant regulator within 24 hours of becoming aware of it, with a preliminary incident report within 5 business days and a complete investigation report within 30 days. Other thermal incidents presenting a credible fire or injury risk must be reported to the regulator within 5 business days. Manufacturers must promptly notify affected customers when an incident indicates a material safety risk, and in any event within 5 business days of confirming that risk. Reports must include available unit, model, installation, and incident details; updates must be submitted as investigations progress."
