   "rule_summary": "The maximum permitted failure rate is 7% of tested units per model. Customers considering or purchasing a model must receive that model's numerical result, sample size, compliance status, material safety risks, and relevant corrective actions; these results need not be published to the general public.",
   "comparison": "weakened by: permanent_limit_pct",
   "final_rule_text": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C before market entry and at least annually thereafter, using a regulator-accepted protocol and a representative sample. The maximum permitted failure rate is 7% of tested units per model. Manufacturers must provide each model’s numerical result, sample size, testing methodology, and corrective actions to regulators. Customers considering or purchasing a model must receive that model’s numerical result, sample size, compliance status, material safety risks, and relevant corrective actions; these results need not be published to the general public. A model exceeding the limit may not be newly installed until it passes a confirmatory test and the regulator accepts its corrective-action plan."
  },
