   "comparison": "weakened by: new_unit_deadline_months",
   "final_rule_text": "New units must include a secure remote emergency shut-off capability no later than 24 months after this standard takes effect, with a safe local means of operation retained. For units already installed, manufacturers must provide a retrofit or equivalent upgrade within 6 years of the effective date where technically feasible. Shut-off must be available to authorized emergency responders and the customer, with safeguards against unauthorized activation; manufacturers must communicate any limitations and safe manual shut-off instructions."
